hadiths[55]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2538","Abu Marah, the freed slave of Aqeel bin Abi Talib, said: He heard from Sayyidah Umm Hani bint Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with her: She narrates that she went to the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the year of the conquest of Makkah, and said: O Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace! My mother's brother-in-law (Sayyidna Ali bin Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him)) thinks that he will kill such and such son of Habira, whom I have sheltered. The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \O Umm Hani! To whom you have given refuge"
"2539","Ibn Mu'iz Saadi said: I went out to get fodder for my horse and I passed by one of the mosques of Banu Hanifa. I came back to Sayyidna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (RA) and informed him about it, so Sayyidna Ibn Mas'ud (RA) sent the police to those people, they caught him, they brought him. The people repented and returned to their word, Sayyiduna Ibn Mas'ud Radiyallahu Anhu cleared their way (i.e. left them). A man came from among them, who was called Abdullah bin Nawaha, and he was killed by Sayyidna Ibn Mas'ud, may Allah be pleased with him. The people said to him: You left all the people and killed him? Sayyiduna Ibn Mas'ud (RA) replied that I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) when he and another person came as a delegation from Musailmah, and the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said to them: \Do you both bear witness that I am the Messenger of Allah?\"" They both said: Do you bear witness that Musailmah is the Messenger of Allah? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""I believe in Allah and His messengers. If I were to kill the delegation (messengers)"
"2540","It was narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Bakr that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Whoever kills a covenanter (dhimmi) without reason"
"2541","Sayyidna Imran bin Hussain (RA) said: Uzba's camel belonged to a man from Banu Uqil who was taken prisoner and the camel was seized. The Messenger of Allah (SAW) passed by it while it was tied up. The man said: O Muhammad! In what crime have you people caught me and the camel walking in front of the pilgrims even though I have become a Muslim? The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \If you had confessed to being a Muslim when you were free"
"2542","Sayyidna Abu Huraira (RA) said: I was with Sayyidna Ali bin Abi Talib (RA) when he was sent (to Makkah) by the Messenger of Allah (PBUH), he announced four things until his voice became full: Listen, people! Only the soul of a Muslim will enter Paradise, and after this year, no polytheist will ever perform Hajj, and no naked person will circumambulate the house of Allah."
"2543","Sayyidna Bara bin Azib, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, put on the Ihram of Umrah in the month of Dhu Qa'dah, but the people of Mecca did not allow him, may God bless him and grant him peace, to enter Mecca. Finally, the peace was reached on the basis that he, may God bless him and grant him peace, would stay in Mecca for three days next year. If we know that you are the Messenger of Allah, we will not stop you at all. You are only Muhammad, the son of Abdullah. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: I am the Messenger of Allah and Muhammad bin Abdullah. He, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, wrote instead of the Messenger of Allah: This is the document on which Muhammad bin Abdullah made peace on the condition that he would not enter Makkah with his sword in its sheath, and if a person from Makkah wanted to go with him, he would not take him with him, but if someone from among his Companions wanted to stay in Makkah, they would not stop him. In the following year, when he (PBUH) visited Makkah and the period of three days was completed, the polytheists of Makkah came to Sayyiduna Ali (RA) and said: Tell your Sahib that the period is completed and now leave Makkah."
"2544","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) said: Two slaves ran away from Taif to the Prophet (PBUH). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) freed them, one of them was Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"2545","Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) said: Sayyidna Sa’d bin Mu’adh (RA) was struck by an arrow in the battle of the factions and his vein (named Abjal) was cut, which the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) burned with fire. When Sayyiduna Sa'd saw this situation (and became certain of death), he said: O Allah, do not take my life until my eyes cool from Banu Qurayzah (i.e. I see their death by the will of Allah), their veins stopped and not a single drop of blood dripped from it until Banu Qurayzah came down at the command of Sayyidna Sa'd bin Mu'adh Rady Allahu Anhu (i.e. they surrendered). A message was sent to Sayyidna Sa'd (may Allah be pleased with him) (i.e. he called them, they came) and Sayyidna Sa'd (may Allah be pleased with him) decided: Their men should be killed and their women kept alive so that the Muslims would be helped by them. The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \You have decided about them according to the decision of Allah.\"" At that time"
"2546","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Adi bin Hamra Zahri (RA) said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) riding in Jazura (the name of a place in Makkah). He (PBUH) was saying: \By Allah (O Makkah)"
"2547","Umm al-Momineen Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Do not speak ill of the dead"
"2548","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) said: On the day of the conquest of Makkah, the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \There is no migration (from Makkah) after this conquest"
"2549","Abu Hind Bijli, who was among the righteous Salaf, said that people mentioned Hijrah to Sayyiduna Muawiya, may Allah be pleased with him, while he was on his throne. He said: I heard the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: \Hijrah will not cease until repentance ceases.\"" Three times he"
"2550","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \If there had been no migration"
"2551","It was narrated on the authority of Sayyidina Abu Huraira that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Whoever is the ruler of ten men"
"2552","Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Beware of oppression"
"2553","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said that the Prophet (PBUH) said: \Indeed"
"2554","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Muawiyah bin Abi Sufyan (RA) that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) stood among us in the form of a preacher and said: \Listen! Before you"
"2555","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said: \Whoever sees something that he dislikes from his Amir"
"2556","Iyas bin Salama narrated from his father, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \The person who takes up arms against us is not one of us.\"""""""
"2557","Imam al-Zuhri (may God have mercy on him) said: Muhammad bin Jubayr bin Mut'am used to narrate hadith from Sayyiduna Mu'awiyah (may God be pleased with him) at that time Muhammad was with him in the delegation of Quraish. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: \This caliphate will remain in the Quraish and whoever is hostile to them"
"2558","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \Quraysh and Ansar"
"2559","On the authority of Sayyidina Abu Bakrah, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Tell me"
"2560","Sayyiduna Abu Dharr, may Allah be pleased with him, said that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said: \May Allah forgive them and the tribe of Islam"
"2561","It was narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (RA) that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \May Allah forgive them"
"2562","Narrated by Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him. He said: Yes, there is no covenant in Islam (i.e. such an agreement that persecution and truth will help in both situations) and the covenants and covenants that used to be in Jahiliyya, Islam has made it stricter and more serious."
"2563","Shu'ba said: I asked Mu'awiya bin Qura: Did Sayyiduna Anas (RA) narrate that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said to Nu'man bin Muqrin: \The son of a nation's sister is a member of the nation.\"" Said: Yes."""""
"2564","Kathir bin Abdullah narrated from his father, his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \The master of the nation is from among them"
"2565","Sayyiduna Amr bin Al-Khajri (RA) said: I was with the camel of the Messenger of Allah (PBUH), I heard him say: \Whoever becomes the son of someone other than his father or a slave to someone other than his master due to resentment"
"2566","Sayyidna Sa'd and Sayyidna Abu Bakrah (RA) narrated the hadith that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \Whoever claims kinship to someone other than his father"
"2567","Sayyidna Nu'man bin Basheer (RA) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) saying: \Halal is clear and what is forbidden is also clear. Between them"
"2568","Abu Hurairah Saadi said: I asked Sayyiduna Hasan bin Ali (RA): What do you remember from the Messenger of Allah (PBUH)? He said: A man asked you about a problem that I do not know. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) replied: \Leave that which is doubtful for that which is not doubtful.\"""""""
"2569","On the authority of Sayyidna Wabsa bin Mabad Asadi, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Wabsa: \You have come to ask about good and bad?\"" I said: Yes. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) put his fingers together and hit them on the chest and said: \""Ask your soul and your heart. Goodness is that which the soul is satisfied with and there is no hesitation in the heart"
"2570","Abu Hurrah al-Raqashi narrated from his uncle, he says: I was holding the camel’s head of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) during the days of Tashreeq, and I was driving people away from him. Take the original wealth) do not do wrong and do not be wronged.\"" 2571"""""
"2571","(Marfu' Hadith) Isma'il ibn Aban informed us, Hatim ibn Isma'il ibn Aban narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Jabir ibn 'Abdullah (ra), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) cursed the consumer of usury (riba) and its payer."
"2572","On the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \A time will come upon the people"
"2573","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \The best thing is for a man to eat from the earnings of his hands"
"2574","Ismail bin Ubaid bin Rafa'ah narrated from his father, from his grandfather (Raf'a), that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, went to Baqi, and said: \O community of merchants!\"" When they all turned towards him"
"2575","On the authority of Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \A truthful"
"2576","Sayyiduna Jarir bin Abdullah (RA) said: I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) to pray, pay Zakat, and wish good to every Muslim."
"2577","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed over a pile of grain (food) in the market of Medina. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the grain seller: \There is no cheating among Muslims"
"2578","On the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) said: \On the Day of Resurrection there will be a flag for every cheater. It will be said: This is the cheat of so-and-so (so that people will know his cheater).\"""""""
"2579","Sayyidna Muammar bin Abdullah bin Nafi' bin Nadla Al-Adwi, may God be pleased with him, said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say twice: \Nobody hoards except the wrongdoer.\"""""""
"2580","It was narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Umar that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \He who brings wealth from outside will be provided with sustenance"
"2581","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: During the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the prices increased greatly, so the people said: O Messenger of Allah! Prices have gone up, can you set the prices for us? The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Allah is the Creator"
"2582","Sayyiduna Huzaifa Ibn Al-Iman (RA) narrated: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \Angels came to the soul of a person from the previous nations before you (at the time of death) and asked"
"2583","On the authority of Sayyiduna Hakeem bin Hizam, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \The buyer and the seller have the right (to cancel the sale) until the two are separated"
"2584","(Marfu' Hadith) Abu al-Walid informed us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah, with its chain, like it (i.e., the same hadith as above)."
"2585","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) saying: \When there is a dispute between the seller and the buyer (buyer and seller) and the seller (i.e. the goods) is present and there is no evidence (or witness) between the two"
"2586","Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Aamir (RA) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) saying: \It is not permissible for a person who believes in Allah and the Last Day to make a bargain (bai') on the bargain (bai') of his brother until he (the other brother) abandons the bargain.\"""""""
"2587","It was narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Aamir (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \The authority (i.e. guarantee) for a slave is three days.\"""""""
"2588","Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Aamir (RA) said: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \The guarantee of a slave is for three days.\"" \n Qatadah"
"2589","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Whoever buys a goat or a camel that has collected milk"
"2590","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (SAW) forbade Baya Gharr (a pledge of deceit)."
"2591","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (SAW) forbade the sale of fruits before they were ripe. He prohibited both the seller and the buyer from this sale."
"2592","It was narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Jabir that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Whoever sells (buys) a fruit and then a calamity befalls it (fruit)"
